\tag{fdip}
\title{Direction algebras of homogeneous calculi}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{A conjugation-stable set of direction labels generates a twisted
group algebra. On an elementary abelian group of exponent #{2} that
algebra is the Clifford algebra of the derived form. On an abelian
group of exponent at least #{3} it is the commutative group algebra.
On the binary tetrahedral group it is the group algebra of order
#{24}.}

